<h1>About</h1>
<p class="lead">I'm Himanshu Sardana — a developer who lives in the terminal. Arch (i3 / Hyprland), Neovim, and a mild obsession with fast, minimal software.</p>
<div class="about-box prose">
<p>I build <b>developer tools and systems projects</b>: a Kafka clone in Go (<a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/camus">camus</a>), a TUI manga reader (<a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/manga-tui">manga-tui</a>), a static site generator (<a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/kite">kite</a>), a minimal git frontend (<a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/bonsai">bonsai</a>), and competitive-programming tooling (<a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/cpos">cpos</a>).</p>
<p>Day to day: <b>Go, Python, TypeScript/Svelte</b>. Also comfortable with Tauri, SQLite, ChromaDB, and LLM APIs (Groq, Gemini).</p>
<p>Find me on <a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana">GitHub @HimanshuSardana</a> · blog at <a href="https://himanshu.co">himanshu.co</a>.</p>
</div>
